From d6573869e524dc81c3054293c8361ac1b25e6cc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:23:20 +0000
Subject: 88W8964: don't claim mgmt frame CCMP header and MIC are stripped

When the 88W8964 firmware passes up a protected management frame, it
has decrypted the frame in place but left the 8-byte CCMP header and
the 8-byte MIC around the body. For example, a 4-byte BSS Transition
Management Query arrived as a 44-byte frame:

  24-byte header | 01 00 00 20 00 00 00 00 | 0a 06 05 06 | 8-byte MIC

The driver nevertheless reports RX_FLAG_IV_STRIPPED and
RX_FLAG_MMIC_STRIPPED, so mac80211 skips its own CCMP processing and
parses the CCMP header as the start of the frame body. Every protected
management frame from a station is misread this way: the query above
was seen as category 1 (QoS) action 0, block ack action frames were not
recognized, and protected deauthentication and disassociation frames
were parsed with a bogus reason code.

For management frames, report only RX_FLAG_DECRYPTED, so that mac80211
removes the CCMP header and MIC itself (and checks the PN against
replays).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
---
 hif/pcie/8964/rx_ndp.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8964/rx_ndp.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8964/rx_ndp.c
@@ -369,10 +369,17 @@ static inline void pcie_rx_process_slow_
 			    is_multicast_ether_addr(wh->addr1) ||
 			    (ieee80211_is_mgmt(wh->frame_control) &&
 			    !is_multicast_ether_addr(wh->addr1))) {
-				if (!ieee80211_is_auth(wh->frame_control))
+				if (!ieee80211_is_mgmt(wh->frame_control))
 					status->flag |= RX_FLAG_IV_STRIPPED |
 							RX_FLAG_DECRYPTED |
 							RX_FLAG_MMIC_STRIPPED;
+				else if (!ieee80211_is_auth(wh->frame_control))
+					/* The firmware decrypts protected
+					 * management frames in place, but
+					 * leaves the CCMP header and MIC for
+					 * mac80211 to remove.
+					 */
+					status->flag |= RX_FLAG_DECRYPTED;
 			}
 		}
 
